<SiteLayout title="Merchants" description="Merchant controls and attribution protections in HonorCart."><PageHero eyebrow="For merchants" title="Coupon help with fewer attribution surprises." lead="HonorCart is being built to respect merchant terms, preserve existing referrals, and give operators direct control over monetized behavior."/><section class="section shell"><div class="three-grid"><article class="plain-card"><h3>Merchant-specific controls</h3><p>Coupon testing, referral detection, checkout-value observation, and monetization can each be configured independently.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h3>Fail-safe behavior</h3><p>Missing or stale policy means stand down. Monetization is permitted only when server policy explicitly allows it.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h3>Documented escalation</h3><p>Merchants can report incompatibility or request immediate deactivation while a behavior is reviewed.</p></article></div></section><section class="callout shell"><h2>Need HonorCart disabled on your store?</h2><p>Contact us with your verified merchant domain. The data model includes an immediate merchant-level kill switch.</p><a href="mailto:merchants@honorcart.com">merchants@honorcart.com →</a></section></SiteLayout>
